  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Innovation Window: Bangladesh Energy Access to Modernisation (BEAM) Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The &quot;Bangladesh Energy Access to Modernisation Fund (BEAM Fund)&quot; project was implemented in Gazipur and Jhenaidah districts of Bangladesh.The BEAM Fund project tested the effectiveness of conditional demand-side subsidies to consumers, to improve the effectiveness of financing in reaching vulnerable market segments. The innovation was modelled on SNV&apos;s global track record and expertise in the delivery of Results-Based Financing (RBF), while integrating elements of retrofit and conditional cash transfer design principles to enhance a market-driven approach for socially inclusive use of demand-side subsidies.Over a period of 18 months, the innovation project impacted circa 7,500 people with clean cooking access accross 1,500 households. The BEAM Fund project provided approximately &#x20AC;30,000 in demand-side subsidies to consumers.The innovation is aligned with the Government of Bangladesh&apos;s (GoB) priorities to promote stove stacking practices to achieve universal access to clean cooking by 2030.</narrative>
  </description>
